      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-06-16_WidnesExaminer_art0010" n="art0010">
        <head>M cDOTTGAL 1:S PATENT SELF—RAISING FLOUR MAKES THE BEST PASTRY.</head>
        <p>M cDOTTGAL 1:S PATENT SELF—RAISING FLOUR MAKES THE BEST PASTRY.</p>
        <p>RESULTS OF BOOTS, CASH CHEMIST'S SPRING CLEANING COMPETITIONS (SCHOOL PHizEs). ENGLISH COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>For the two best compositions on Spring Cleaning, written by any pupil ender 18 years of age and atten.ling any Ele- mentary Public School or Continuation School. has been awarded to GEORGE LAMB of Hatfield aSti road Board School, St. Albans. Age of Competitor 9.</p>
        <p>Standard 5,</p>
        <p>Sne, Q has been awarded to AN F. BULL of the Nationa V Mixed School, Leamington Spa. Age of Competitor 13. Standard 6.</p>
        <p>ENGLISH COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>For the two best letters on Spring Cleaning sent in by a pupil not higher than the 4th Standard in any Elementary Public School-</p>
        <p>gc, has been awarded to ELLEN SHARP of the Garden t) Fields Board School, St. Albans, Herts. Age of Competitor 11. Standard 4. has been awarded to CONSTANCE ELLA DAVIS hi of Bedford-road Board School, Bootle, Liverpool. Age of Competitor 9. Standard 2. FRENCH AND GERMAN COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>Whilst competitns freely came in for the English Cone position prizes, those in French or German we re very small in number. and for the roost part poor in quality. The competitions were advertised over a very wide area-85 towns—in addition.to such large cities as Manchester, Liver- pool, Birmingham, ao.. having altogether a total population of many millions. The only one sent in from a Board School was received from a pupil of Huntingdon-street Board School, Nottingham: Corouaring the number of replies received for various English competitions and those for competitions in French or Germrn, it would appear that a most unsatis- factory percentage of the pupils even in the highest standards of the Board and National Schools have any practical knowledge whatever of French or German. gshas been awarded to MARY' ELIZABETH LAWSON, Huntington-street Board Schoal, Nottingham, for a otter in French. Age of Competitor 16. We are unable to award the second and third prizes in connection with this competition. FRENCH AND GERMAN COMPETITIONS.— PRIVATE SCHOOLS.</p>
        <p>has been awarded to VIOLET JONES. pupil Leigh (kit/ Bank College,Leamington Spa.for a letter in French. Age of Competitor 16. id) has been awarden OLIVIA LAMB, of St. Albans, 4.. d 56, of whose pupils forwarded competition letters. 1:1 has been awarded, as an extra prize, to H. SHAW, of 1 the Girls' British School Gloucester, 50 of Whose pupils sent in competitions. HOUSE CLEANING. No need to smother your rooms with stuffy carpets ! No need of French polishers 1 Everything may be done decently and in order by the lady of the house I</p>
        <p>USE BOOTS VARNISH STAINS which give a brilliant polish in Oak, Wvlnut, Mahogany, &amp;c. Staining and Varnishing Woodwork at one operation. Usual 6d. size for 4.0., is. size for Bd., and 2s. 6d. size for Is. sd. per bottle. :NIORGAN'S GOLD AND SILVER PAINT A 3 used by Cabinet Makers, Gilders, and Decorators. Has the original brightness of Gold, easy of application, and unrivalled in appearance. Boots reduced price, Is. bottle for 74d. UNRIVALLED METAL POLISH</p>
        <p>BOOTS BRASS PASTE OR METAL PoLisH will clean every hind of metal, brass, steel, or iron, and is invaluable in household use. Trial size, usual 2d. for id., ls. Tin for 4d.</p>
        <p>WILLS' CLEANSING CLOUDY AMMONIA is. size for 10d. Small trial size 6d.</p>
        <p>HOUSEMAIDS' GLOVES, WASH LEATHERS, FURNI- TURE CEYAM, SOFT SOAP, VARN.SH STAINS, BRUNSWICK BLACK, ac., &amp;c.. Ac., of the best quality are sold at the lowest prices.</p>
