        <p>Oti Friday night a man named Martin Collins, residing at Latchford, was drowned whilst bathing in the Bridgewater Canal near Pickering's Bridge, The!wall. Ile was seized with cramp, cud before assistance arrive, was drowned. The inquest was held on Saturday, by Mr. H. C. Yates, county coroner, at the Picluring Arms, Thelwall, and a verdict of '• Death by drowning" was returned. The Medical Profession recornmsni the moderate use of well niatin,d PORT WINN in cases of Influenza. W. and A. GILBEY have speciailsr selected the finest Wine front Oporto for this purpose end thus placed their 3.000 Agents in la position to supply their Invalid Port, at 2s. 6d per bottle in.wery town.—Advt.</p>
