      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-06-16_WidnesExaminer_art0065" n="art0065">
        <head>WORD TO THE WISE.</head>
        <p>A WORD TO THE WISE.</p>
        <p>The fickle nature of the climate of this country of en gives rise Vs a variety of ailments and complai.nts,which assuming at first the form of only a slight indisposition, neglected and unheeded may 132 c )me the germ of serious diseases, which will andermine the constitution, and finally result in a long and lingering illaess,and per- haps terminate fatally. The variable temperature and the changeable weatlev r of the last month sr so, makes it incumbent on al of us to excrcir wi,e and prudent precautions to counteract the evil effects which the weather may have had upon our health and ocin fort. Already we frpquAntly hear such c)mplaints es " No appetite." '6 Thse frFcpenl: headaches," " This n- guid feeling," and dozens of other expressions which all point to the urgent need of a good Tonic. Nlw tt re are several tonic mix:ures offered t 3 the Public, ut none which have been so uniforrnlr successful as Gsvilyrn Evans Quinine Bitters, The Vegetable Tonic. This preparation is acknowledged to be The Best Remedy of the Age fir Nervousnss, Weakness, Chest Affections, Palpitaf-ion of the Heart, Indigestion, Liver Complaint, and Influenza.</p>
        <p>The numerous cases of marvellous cures effected, and the restoratiln to perfect health, of those who had long suffered and had vainly tried other rem,dies, can be accounted f3r by simply s atiug the effect which Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters has up3n the System. - -</p>
        <p>Ist. It strik,ls at the source of the dlsease, and by removing the causes of dislase, the evil effects soon vanish. - -</p>
        <p>------- 2nd. It strengthens that part of the system which is weakest, and therefore, most liable to the attacks of colds and all diseases. 3rd: L 7, purifies the blood, and thus gives new life and force to all parss of the body, for disease cannot exist where there is a free circulation of pure blood. 4th. It gives healthy action to the digestive organs, and to the liver, thui ai.ling to keep away Indigestion, and the host of different forms of disease which result rum it. •</p>
        <p>sth. By removing impurities,strengthening the weak parts of the system, and purifying the b;o3d, the human frame is well fortified to withstand the atticks of dis- ease. It is repelled, and its place taken by health and strength, through the effective action of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, Toe Vi,etable Tonic. Sold everywhere in bottles 2s. 9d. and 43. 6 L each, or will be sent car- riage free for these prices, direct from the Sole Proprie- tors :—Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited,Lhinelly, South Wales. Beware of Imitations. See that you get the genuine Preparation with the name, "Gwilym Evans" on Label, Stamp, and Bottle, without which none is genuine.</p>
